Below is a practical, step‑by‑step guide you can follow to build a modern, production‑ready frontend for an e‑commerce site.  
I’ll cover the whole stack – from design to deployment – and give you concrete choices, folder layouts, and code snippets so you can jump straight into coding.

---

## 1️⃣  Define the Scope & User Flows

| Feature | Description | Typical UI |
|---------|-------------|------------|
| **Home / Landing** | Hero banner, featured products, categories | Carousel + grid |
| **Product Listing** | Category view, filters, sorting, pagination | Masonry / grid |
| **Product Detail** | Images, description, price, reviews, add‑to‑cart | Tabs + image gallery |
| **Cart** | Summary, quantity changes, remove | Sidebar or modal |
| **Checkout** | Shipping address, payment, order review | Multi‑step wizard |
| **Account** | Login / signup, order history, profile | Tabs |
| **Admin** | Product CRUD, order management | Dashboard |

Sketch wireframes in Figma/Sketch first; keep them low‑fidelity to iterate quickly.

---

## 2️⃣  Pick a Tech Stack

| Layer | Recommendation | Why |
|-------|----------------|-----|
| **Framework** | **Next.js** (React) | SSR + SSG, file‑based routing, built‑in API routes |
| **State** | **React Query** + **Zustand** | Server state + global UI state |
| **Styling** | **Tailwind CSS** + **Headless UI** | Utility‑first, easy theming |
| **Component Library** | **Radix UI** (accessibility) | Headless primitives |
| **Payments** | **Stripe Elements** | PCI‑compliant, easy to integrate |
| **Auth** | **NextAuth.js** | OAuth + email magic links |
| **Testing** | **Jest + React Testing Library** + **Cypress** | Unit + E2E |
| **CI/CD** | **GitHub Actions** + **Vercel** | Deploy preview + production |
| **Analytics** | **Google Analytics** + **Mixpanel** | User behavior |
| **Monitoring** | **Sentry** | Runtime errors |
| **Performance** | **Image Optimization** (next/image), **Code Splitting** | Fast load times |
| **Accessibility** | **axe-core** + **Storybook** | WCAG compliance |
| **Internationalization** | **next-i18next** | Multi‑language support |
| **PWA** | **next-pwa** | Offline, installable |

> **Why Next.js?**  
> It gives you SSR for SEO, SSG for static pages, and API routes for a lightweight backend—all in one repo.

---

