### Quick Start Code Snippet

```tsx
// pages/index.tsx
import { useProducts } from '@/hooks/useProducts';
import { ProductCard } from '@/components/product/Card';

export default function Home() {
  const { data, isLoading } = useProducts();

  if (isLoading) return <p>Loading...</p>;

  return (
    <div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 p-4">
      {data?.map((p) => (
        <ProductCard key={p.id} product={p} />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}
```

Run locally:

```bash
npm run dev
```

Open `http://localhost:3000` and you’re ready to iterate.

---

### Final Thought

Building a full‑featured e‑commerce frontend is a marathon, not a sprint. Keep the code modular, test often, and iterate on user feedback. With the stack above, you’ll have a scalable, maintainable, and delightful shopping experience. Happy coding!
